  "observations": [
    "The invalid form shows the empty red input border, complete Chinese validation, cancel action and disabled submit; the held-save view shows disabled controls and retained name.",
    "The ordinary save-error and stale-source views show complete Chinese error text, retained names and retry/cancel actions. The cancel-focus view does not show a blue keyboard outline, so that PNG alone does not prove keyboard focus return.",
    "The registered-light view is scrolled to preferences and shows the full disabled-auto-cleanup count explanation. It does not show the newly registered row; durable registration is established by native assertions and the six later layout views.",
    "The restore-restart view shows the root controls and upstream/cleanup settings; lower controls require vertical scrolling.",
    "All six light/dark 100/125/150-percent form images show the name and cancel/submit controls with the complete blue keyboard focus ring on submit. At 150 percent the branch heading and lower sidebar categories need their independent vertical scrolling.",
    "All six corresponding error images show the complete storage error and retained name with visible cancel/retry actions; at 150 percent the error wraps to two lines. These error PNGs do not show a blue outline on submit."
  ],
